{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1247799-ubiquitous-things-an-immaculate-fable","id":1247799,"title":"Ubiquitous Things (An Immaculate Fable)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-19T13:51:06-07:00","id":1247799,"title":"Ubiquitous Things (An Immaculate Fable)","content":"<div align=\"center\">HOW IS IT THAT THE TEN UBIQUITOUS THINGS WERE GIVEN TO HUMANITY?: AN IMMACULATE FABLE</div> <br /> At one time, the Elemental Dragons gathered together and looked at the humans They had made. They saw that humans were hungry, but had nothing to eat. They saw that humans were tired, but had nowhere to rest. They saw that humans desired to build, but had no tools.<br /> <br /> In Their mercy, the Elemental Dragons decided to bestow gifts upon humanity. Among Themselves They decided that each out make two gifts: one a plant, and one an animal. They agreed that They would return in five days and give their gifts to humankind.<br /> <br /> Then each of the Elemental Dragons went to Their corner of the world and shaped a portion of Their own body into a gift. After five days, They returned to the humans and shared Their gifts.<br /> <br /> The Dragon of Earth spoke first. His voice resounded like the striking of temple bells. In one mighty claw He held rice, and in the other He held a pregnant cow.<br /> <br /> <b>I have made Rice,</b> He proclaimed, and sewed rice into Creation. Where the seed struck the fertile earth they grew into rich paddies. <b>With My gift, humanity will never starve. It will grow nutritious and sweet and they will use it to fill their bellies.</b><br /> <br /> <b>I have made Ox,</b> He proclaimed, and set the cow into Creation, where she ate the grass and gave birth to many calves of many kinds. <b>With My gift, humanity will always have labor. Oxen will pull their plows and till their soil so their fields will grow rich.</b><br /> <br /> So humanity was grateful for the Earth Dragon's gifts. They filled their bellies with rice and used oxen to plow their fields, because of His love.<br /> <br /> The Dragon of Air spoke second. Her voice rang out like the jangling of sacred chimes. In one mighty claw She held flax, and in the other she held a mother crane.<br /> <br /> <b>I have made Flax,</b> She proclaimed, and scattered flax into Creation. Where the seeds touched the fertile earth blue fields bloomed. <b>With My gift, humanity will never freeze. It will grow thick and plentiful and they will shape it into cloth.</b><br /> <br /> <b>I have made Bird,</b> She proclaimed, and set the crane into Creation, where she flew in the skies and raised many fledglings of many kinds. <b>With My gift, humanity will always have wonder. Birds will write the future in the sky and embody hope so their minds will think great thoughts.</b><br /> <br /> So humanity was grateful for the Air Dragon\u2019s gifts. They clothed their bodies in linen and scryed the future in the movement of birds because of Her love.<br /> <br /> The Dragon of Wood spoke third. His voice was thick like amber sap from ancient trees. In one mighty claw He held bamboo, and in the other He held a pregnant doe.<br /> <br /> <b>I have made Bamboo, </b>He proclaimed, and loosed it into Creation. Where it touched soil or sand it sprouted towering stalks. <b>With My gift, humanity will never be exposed. It will grow fast and strong and they will build great structures from it.</b><br /> <br /> <b>I have made Deer,</b> He proclaimed, and set the doe into Creation, where she scampered among the trees and birthed many fawns of many kinds. <b>With My gift, humanity will always have guidance. Deer will carve tracks for them through wild places and flee when danger is near so their travels will be safe.</b><br /> <br /> So humanity was grateful for the Wood Dragon\u2019s gifts. They built their homes from dried bamboo and followed the deer through deep nature because of His love.<br /> <br /> The Dragon of Water spoke fourth. Her voice pattered like rain on silent statues. In one mighty claw She held paper reed, and in the other She held a mother carp.<br /> <br /> <b>I have made Sedge,</b> She proclaimed, and tossed it into Creation. Where it took root on water\u2019s edge it grew reached toward the sky. <b>With My gift, humanity will never forget. It will grow bountiful and elegant and they will make it into paper.</b><br /> <br /> <b>I have made Fish,</b> She proclaimed, and set the carp into Creation, where it swam to deepest depths and laid many eggs of many kinds. <b>With My gift, humanity will always have beauty. Fish will shine with glorious scales and clams will make pearls so that they might decorate.</b><br /> <br /> So humanity was grateful for the Water Dragon\u2019s gifts. They made paper from paper reed and made things of beauty from the deep creatures of the sea because of Her love.<br /> <br /> The Dragon of Fire spoke last. His voice crackled like sacred bonfires in distant shrines. In one mighty claw He held tea, and in the other He held a pregnant sow.<br /> <br /> <b>I have made Tea,</b> He proclaimed, and spread tea into Creation, where it grew thick and sweet among the open fields. <b>With My gift, humanity will always have comfort. It will grow rich and flavorful and they will drink of it together.</b><br /> <br /> <b>I have made Swine,</b> He proclaimed, and set the sow into Creation, where she rooted in the earth and gave birth to many sucklings. <b>With My gift, humanity will always have plenty. Swines will grow fat and delicious so they will feast and be merry.</b><br /> <br /> So humanity was grateful for the Fire Dragon\u2019s gifts. They drank tea in community and banqueted on pork and meats because of His love.<br /> <br /> Thus it came to pass that the Ten Ubiquitous Gifts were bestowed upon humanity. Even today, these ten things are found through all corners of Creation. Wherever plants grow, humanity will find rice, flax, bamboo, sedge, and tea. Wherever animals roam, humanity will find oxen, birds, deer, fish and swine. This is because the gifts of the Elemental Dragons are to be found in all corners of Creation.<br /> <br /> When you eat rice, or weave cloth, or shape bamboo, or write or read, or drink tea, think of the mercy of the Elemental Dragons who love humanity so. When you drive oxen, watch birds, hunt deer, catch fish, or feast on pork, think of the mercy of the Elemental Dragons who love humanity so. It is through Them that these gifts were given to humanity.<br /> <hr /><br /> Last night I had a conversation with some other folks on the Exalted Discord, spawned by a comment I made that <i>rice and tea </i>were present in almost all parts of Creation in the games I run. For me, I almost immediately assume that any given town in Creation will have a tea house, and most people eat rice as a staple crop.<br /> <br /> From there, we discussed the associations between the various major deities (Elemental Dragons, Incarnae, etc) and various plants and animals. In the end, I felt inspired to write a short Immaculate fable that would explain why some plants and animals are to be found throughout Creation.<br /> <br /> Along the way I ended up with some interesting conclusions. Flax, for instance, is a blue-budding plant that grows in colder climates and makes cloth, so it seems natural it would be associated with Mela and the element of Air. I also like the idea that papyrus can be connected to Water because it relates to the themes of bureaucracy and memory that are associated with Water and Danaa'd.<br /> <br /> I hope you enjoy my writing!, or at least find it interesting. I tried to draw on some stylistic elements from my own religious background, so the text has a lot of repetition and parallelism. Hopefully those are more interesting than they are distracting. If you're inspired to leave any comments I'd love to hear them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24333-electronsutra","name":"ElectronSutra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24333_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T09:35:17-07:00","id":1248106,"title":"","content":"Of course. preachers quickly learned to adapt the Ubiquitous Things depending on Direction.<br /> <br /> &quot;Th'fuck's a bamboof?&quot;<br /> <br /> - Chipped Bowl, Gemite potter.<br /> <br /> Which means that in the South, the immaculate faithful say Sextes Jylis granted the gift of marijuana - to ease the suffering of man, and they praise Mela for granting them shelter, because flax makes straw, and straw makes adobe brick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}